coder › Implemented the token bucket in `src/limiter.ts` and expanded the tests in `src/limiter.test.ts`.

What changed
- `src/limiter.ts`:
  - Added private `#tokens` and `#lastRefill` state; the bucket starts full (`tokens = capacity`, `lastRefill = now()`).
  - `#refill()` adds `elapsedSeconds * refillPerSecond` and clamps to `capacity` (and ignores a clock that moves backwards).
  - `tryTake(n = 1)` refills, refuses `n > capacity` outright, returns `false` without taking anything when tokens are insufficient, otherwise deducts `n` and returns `true`.
  - `available` refills up to the current time and returns the (possibly fractional) token count.
- `src/limiter.test.ts`: kept the existing "starts full" test and added tests for insufficient-token refusal (taking nothing), fractional refill, continuous refill capped at capacity, and `n > capacity` always being refused.

